  "batch_id": "sora-ichikawa-cortex-eddie-palmieri-2026-08-29-discovery",
  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass completed on 2026-08-29 after rereading the current docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, and radar/inbox/README.md from main. Fresh Yamamoto checks of Jazz House ALFIE, BODY&SOUL, schedule traces, Space M&A leads, and credible Japanese-jazz sources produced no new verified unrecorded Yamamoto performance with a performance-specific reason that cleared Stage 1; already-curated Yamamoto dates were not duplicated. The broader pass admitted three unrecorded performances for specific live-context reasons: Sora Ichikawa's release performance returns the Concept Band to ALFIE, the room where its first live album was recorded; Cortex brings Alain Mion's founder-led French psychedelic jazz-funk project to a local Washington date on the Le Jazz Est Mort North American tour; and Jazz at Lincoln Center convenes longtime Eddie Palmieri collaborators and alumni for a two-night all-star celebration. Priority was assigned only after admission. Final proposed distribution: A 1, A+ 2, S 0, S+ 0. The recent/current RADAR intake remains centered on A and A+, with S/S+ sparse; this batch preserves that shape without using a quota. Cortex was not promoted to S because the 2026 itinerary is a multi-city North American tour and the group also toured North America in 2024. The Eddie Palmieri Experience was not promoted to S because the November program runs two nights and follows a related Palmieri retrospective at the January 2026 Unity Jazz Festival; active prioritization is more durable than a one-off scarcity claim. No automated self-check is represented as independent Codex or human review.",
